# Development Guidelines

## Project Guidelines

### Content Guidelines
- Keep README minimal and to the point
- Don't use non-ASCII characters anywhere
- Focus on essential information only
- Use simple, clear language

### Technical Guidelines
- Use ASCII-only characters in all files
- Keep workflows minimal for initial testing
- Migration scripts should be added later, not in initial setup
- Focus on core functionality first

### File Structure
- Keep repository structure simple
- Only create directories when needed
- Use existing working components as foundation
- Maintain compatibility with existing local-dev setup

### Commit Guidelines
- User will handle commits manually
- Focus on implementation, not git operations
- Test changes before suggesting commits

### Workflow Guidelines
1. Start with minimal working setup
2. Test GitHub Actions workflow
3. Add complexity incrementally
4. Keep migration and advanced features for later phases

### Security Guidelines
- Use GitHub Secrets for sensitive data
- Never commit secrets to repository
- Use environment variables for configuration
- Follow security best practices

### Performance Guidelines
- Keep response times under 400ms
- Use Docker for containerization
- Leverage existing working components
- Test locally before deployment

## Future Enhancement Guidelines
- Add Jekyll migration only after basic setup works
- Implement Supabase integration in later phases
- Add AI features incrementally
- Maintain backward compatibility

## Testing Guidelines
- Test local-dev setup first
- Verify GitHub Actions workflow
- Test deployment manually before automation
- Keep testing simple and focused
